---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="What Is Permanent Jewelry? — HUE Co." description="Permanent jewelry explained: no clasp, a micro-weld holds your chain closed. Sized to your body, stays on until you choose to remove it. Always free removal.">

<!-- ── Hero ──────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
<section class="section--dark article-hero">
  <div class="container container--narrow">
    <span class="eyebrow eyebrow--light">Permanent Jewelry Explained</span>
    <h1 class="section-title section-title--xl article-hero__title">What Is Permanent Jewelry?</h1>
    <div class="article-hero__meta">
      <span class="article-meta__cat">Basics</span>
      <span class="article-meta__sep">&middot;</span>
      <span class="article-meta__read">7 min read</span>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ── Article Body ───────────────────────────────────────────── -->
<section class="section section--cream">
  <div class="container container--narrow">
    <article class="article-body">

      <h2 class="article-h2">The Short Answer</h2>
      <p>No clasp. A micro-weld holds your chain closed. It's sized to your exact body — your wrist circumference, your ankle, your neck — and it stays on until you remove it. Removal is free, always, and takes less than sixty seconds.</p>
      <p>That's the technical answer. The experiential answer is something different: it's jewelry that feels like it belongs to you. Not borrowed, not adjustable, not lost in the bottom of a bag. Yours. Permanently.</p>

      <h2 class="article-h2">How the Welding Works</h2>
      <p>A professional uses a small micro-welding tool — the same technology jewelers use to size rings and repair fine jewelry. Once the chain is measured and positioned on your body, the welder brings the two ends together and applies a brief pulse of energy. The spark lasts less than a second.</p>
      <p>Nothing touches your skin except the chain itself. There is no heat on your body. No sharp implements. The tool never makes contact with you. Clients who have had the procedure describe the experience as anticlimactic — "I expected more," one client told us. "It was just a small flash, and then it was done."</p>
      <p>Done, and permanent.</p>

      <h2 class="article-h2">Is It Really Permanent?</h2>
      <p>Yes and no. The weld itself is as strong as the rest of the chain — the link we close is indistinguishable from the others. Under normal wear conditions, it won't open.</p>
      <p>But permanence has limits. If your chain gets caught on something and pulled with force — a towel hook, a zipper, a child's grip — the weld may come undone. This is by design: a chain that could withstand that force would be unsafe to wear. The chain breaks before your skin does.</p>
      <p>This is exactly what the 30-day warranty covers. If your weld comes undone within 30 days of your appointment for any reason, we re-weld it for free. After 30 days, re-welds are $20 for Tier 1 and 2, and $35 for Tier 3. Bring both pieces and we'll close it in minutes.</p>

      <h2 class="article-h2">What Metals Are Used?</h2>
      <p>At HUE Co., we work with three metal tiers:</p>
      <ul class="article-list">
        <li><strong>Tier 1 — Stainless Steel PVD:</strong> Physical Vapor Deposition coated stainless steel. The most accessible option. Durable, waterproof, gym-safe, and the entry point into permanent jewelry. From $42.</li>
        <li><strong>Tier 2 — 14k Gold-Filled &amp; Argentium Silver:</strong> Gold-filled is legally required to contain 5% gold by weight — a permanent gold layer that won't flake. Argentium silver is 93.5% pure silver, engineered for tarnish resistance. From $72.</li>
        <li><strong>Tier 3 — 14k Solid Gold:</strong> 58.5% pure gold, alloyed for wearable strength. Available in yellow and white gold. Has real melt value. The investment piece. From $145.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Every tier is waterproof and safe for daily wear. The differences are in the metal composition, the feel, and the price per inch.</p>

      <h2 class="article-h2">Can I Sleep and Shower in It?</h2>
      <p>Yes. That's the entire point. All three metal tiers at HUE Co. are waterproof and safe for daily wear — showering, swimming, sleeping, working out. There are no activities that require removing your piece.</p>
      <p>A few things to be mindful of: rinse with fresh water after extended time in chlorine or salt water, and pat dry after. Avoid leaving your chain in direct contact with harsh chemicals like bleach or acetone. Beyond that, wear it everywhere.</p>

      <h2 class="article-h2">Does It Hurt?</h2>
      <p>No. The spark is quick and targeted — and it doesn't touch your skin. Most clients feel nothing at all. Occasionally clients notice a faint warmth from the chain itself in the seconds after the weld, but this dissipates immediately.</p>
      <p>We've had clients with needle phobias, medical anxiety, and sensory sensitivities complete the process without discomfort. It's genuinely one of the most painless things you can do in a jewelry studio.</p>

      <h2 class="article-h2">Will It Set Off Metal Detectors?</h2>
      <p>Occasionally, depending on the sensitivity of the scanner. The amount of metal in a fine jewelry chain is minimal, and most airport full-body scanners don't react to it. However, older walk-through metal detectors can be more sensitive, and some clients do get flagged.</p>
      <p>This is not a problem. Removal is always free at HUE Co. If you have an MRI scheduled or anticipate issues with security screening, book a removal appointment and we'll have you out of the chair in under sixty seconds. Bring both pieces of the chain and we can re-weld after.</p>

      <div class="article-cta">
        <h3 class="article-cta__title">Ready to Try It?</h3>
        <p class="article-cta__desc">Book your appointment. $25 deposit secures your slot — applied toward your final balance.</p>
        <a href="/book" class="btn btn--gold">Book Your Weld</a>
      </div>

    </article>
  </div>
</section>

